    ("Accretion efficiency in compact binaries", "02-03", "binary_accretion.csv", "compute accretion luminosity for a white dwarf, neutron star, and black hole at a common mass-transfer rate", "Use the shared mdot and masses/radii, propagate a 5% mdot uncertainty, and compare efficiencies.", "OpenStax 24.6 and HEASARC X-ray-binary resources."),
    ("SNR shock and remnant age", "04-05", "snr_shock.csv", "infer shock temperature and age from velocity, angular radius, and distance", "Use a 5,000 km/s shock, 2.0 arcmin radius, and 2.5 kpc distance; report the constant-velocity approximation.", "OpenStax 23.2-23.3 and Chandra SNR resources."),
    ("Pulsar timing and braking", "05-06", "pulsar_timing.csv", "calculate characteristic age, dipole field, and rotational energy loss from timing records", "Use Crab-like P and Pdot values and compare the timing age with a supplied historical age; explain braking-index limitations.", "OpenStax 23.4 Figure 23.16 and NICER documentation."),
    ("Compactness and neutron-star radius", "06-07", "neutron_star_models.csv", "compare mass-radius models with compactness and redshift observables", "Evaluate three model rows at 1.4 Msun and identify how a 10% radius uncertainty changes z.", "NICER About page and OpenStax 24.1."),
    ("Instrument selection for a transient", "11-12", "mission_specs.csv", "select an instrument for a burst using bandpass, response, localization, and reaction-time constraints", "Compare Chandra, NICER, Swift, and Fermi official specifications; do not treat bands as sensitivity curves.", "Official Chandra, NICER, Swift, and Fermi pages listed in reference-log.md."),
